title: Settings › Agents › Arrive and read the sixteen agents
route: /settings
intro: The Settings page is one screen about the agents: who they are, how much freedom each one has, a switch for each, and a button to pause them all, plus a closed card on who can see which site. This shows what the person sees and what each row says.
dir: TD
also: Every level and switch is kept in the app, not in the page. Leave Settings and come back and nothing has changed. 'Reset demo data' puts every agent back to its starting level with its switch on.
---
start s1 "Click 'Settings' in the sidebar\nAbove 'Help', below the 'Demo data' tag"
screen p1 "Settings\nWho the agents are, how much freedom each one has, a way to pause them, and who can see which site."
click hb "Click 'Pause all agents'\nRed outline button, top right\n'Resume all agents' when all sixteen are paused"
goto g1 "Continues in: Settings › Pause › Pause all agents"
toast bn "'Privacy mode is always on'\nNames, dates and IDs are swapped for codes before an agent reads a chart, and mapped back only on your screen."
screen gates "Gates\nAgents never pass these without a person"
screen lv "What each level changes\nOne plain line for each of the three levels\nSubtitle: 'Set per agent. Applied in EMR Connect'"
goto g6 "Continues in: Settings › Agents › What each freedom level allows and the gates it never skips"
goto g2 "Continues in: Settings › Page › Other controls and notices"
screen sa "Sites and access (closed card, first in the grid)\n'Two sites, four roles'"
goto gsa "Continues in: Settings › Sites and access › Read the roles and switch with View as"

group gCov "Coverage"
  screen c0 "Coverage card\nKnows who pays and files with them"
  process c1 "Verify: Checks coverage and benefits\nStarts at 'Act on its own'"
  process c2 "Caller: Makes payer calls\nStarts at 'Ask before acting'"
  process c3 "Navigator: Files and tracks requests\nStarts at 'Act, then report'"
endgroup

group gDoc "Documentation"
  screen d0 "Documentation card\nReads the chart, writes the case"
  process d1 "Reader: Reads the chart, protects identifiers\nStarts at 'Act on its own'"
  process d2 "Criteria: Reviews payer policy"
  process d3 "Placement: Maps the chart to ASAM levels"
  process d4 "Scribe: Drafts the medical-necessity case"
  process d5 "Integrity: Checks every sentence against the chart"
endgroup

group gInt "Intelligence"
  screen i0 "Intelligence card\nKnows how each payer behaves"
  process i1 "Historian: Reviews how this payer has ruled"
  process i2 "Forecaster: Estimates the approval chance"
  process i3 "Sentinel: Watches for policy changes"
  process i4 "Analyst: Answers questions, builds reports"
endgroup

group gCase "Case work"
  screen k0 "Case work card\nMoves each case to done"
  process k1 "Packet: Assembles forms and attachments"
  process k2 "Scrubber: Scrubs requests and claims"
  process k3 "Cadence: Schedules concurrent reviews\nStarts at 'Act, then report'"
  process k4 "Advocate: Handles denials, P2P and appeals"
endgroup

process row "Each row shows\nThe agent's round icon, its name, its role on one line, a Freedom dropdown and an on/off switch\nA 'Paused' tag beside the name while its switch is off"
process st "Every other agent starts at 'Ask before acting'\nAll sixteen switches start on"
click fz "Click a Freedom dropdown"
click sw "Click a switch"
goto g3 "Continues in: Settings › Agents › Change an agent's freedom"
goto g4 "Continues in: Settings › Pause › Pause one agent, resume all"
goto g5 "Continues in: Settings › Agent map › Where each of the sixteen agents works"

s1 --> p1
p1 --> hb --> g1
p1 --> bn
p1 --> c0 & d0 & i0 & k0
c0 --> c1
d0 --> d1
i0 --> i1
k0 --> k1
c1 --> c2 --> c3
d1 --> d2 --> d3 --> d4 --> d5
i1 --> i2 --> i3 --> i4
k1 --> k2 --> k3 --> k4
c3 --> row
d5 --> row
i4 --> row
k4 --> row
row --> st
row --> fz --> g3
row --> sw --> g4
p1 --> sa --> gsa
p1 --> gates --> g2
p1 --> lv --> g6
c1 -.-> g5
